mapping "b270.1" source="b270" target="SNOMED_CT:106148006" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b270 SNOMED CT 106148006 = ICF b270 Sensory functions related to temperature and other
        stimuli: a mid-level grouping spanning temperature sensation (b2700), vibration (b2701),
        pressure, tickle, and other-cutaneous-stimuli senses. No single SNOMED CT standard concept denotes
        this exact sensory grouping. Target SNOMED CT 4024711 (sctid 106148006) =, active standard. Broader
        (multi-level): every b270 sub-function is a sensory function and the target fully subsumes the
        grouping, but it sits well above and covers all sensory functions, not just the
        temperature/other-stimuli axis. Low tier : defensible ancestor lead — the closest standard
        concept to the b270 grouping title — and the enumerated children (b2700 Thermal sensation, b2701
        Vibratory sense) each get their own tighter function-level proposals. Recorded as broader rather
        than no_match because is a defensible term-and-scope match for this sensory sub-grouping.
        """
}
